  "old_exact": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero as an explicit extension of the source Euclidean setting. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and βη≤1. Set μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=Law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd. Let P be the actual conditional-expectation orthogonal projection onto the second-coordinate sigma algebra in L²(J). There exists one linear isometry U:L²(J)→L²(J) whose AE representative is composition with F(x,y)=(x,2x−y), with U²=I and U self-adjoint. Define A=PUP and B=(I−P)UP. For every f∈ran P with ∫f dJ=0, ‖Af‖≤[(1−αη)/(1+αη)]‖f‖ and [4αη/(1+αη)²]‖f‖²≤‖Bf‖². This includes αη=1, uses actual infinite-dimensional L²(J), and is Test-level integration of already produced operators; Γ, its inverse and trajectories are not asserted.",
  "new_exact": "Actual AE pullback range and full centered image; the same actual conditional mean and reflection give the exact sharp contraction and squared defect lower bound for all centered macro inputs, including rank zero and alpha*eta=1. No finite-dimensionality is imposed on real L2.",
  "reason": "Root duplicated the whole statement into current assumption-delta metadata. Corrected lesson and primary restatement did not eliminate this current copy. Replace it with a precise scoped alignment claim without duplicating the theorem or asserting infinite dimension at rank0.",
